{%- comment -%}
  Alterpop — resolves a product's regime. The only place that reads
  alterpop.manufacturer_tier (2026-09-15 briefing, section 3). Four raw
  tier values map to two PDP regimes:
    ARTISAN / SIGNATURE -> premium
    COLLECTOR / CORE / blank / unknown -> impulse

  The exact literal Shopify stores ("ARTISAN" vs. "01 ARTISAN" etc.) is
  unconfirmed on the app side — this snippet accepts only the bare word.
  If the app's format differs, fix it here and nowhere else.

  Params:
    product    (required) — the product to read the tier from.
    force_tier (optional)  — 'impulse' or 'premium', overrides the field
                              (dev preview only, e.g. ?view=premium).

  Outputs: 'premium' or 'impulse' (no trailing whitespace/newline).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign ap_raw = product.metafields.alterpop.manufacturer_tier.value | append: '' | strip | upcase
  assign ap_regime = 'impulse'
  if ap_raw == 'ARTISAN' or ap_raw == 'SIGNATURE'
    assign ap_regime = 'premium'
  endif
  if force_tier == 'impulse' or force_tier == 'premium'
    assign ap_regime = force_tier
  endif
-%}{{ ap_regime }}
